Package: seqsalvage
Title: Import 'Sequencher' Sanger Sequencing Projects
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Ethan", "Bass", email = "ethanbass@uchicago.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Reads 'Sequencher' project files ('.SPF'), extracting each read's
    processed chromatogram traces, base calls, quality scores and peak
    positions, and each contig's name, saved consensus sequence and member
    reads. Can also recover reads and contigs deleted from a project whose data
    remains in the file. Writes reads out as 'ABIF' ('.ab1') trace files and
    contig consensus sequences as 'FASTA'.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Suggests:
    sangerseqR,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.1
URL: https://ethanbass.github.io/seqsalvage/
